This directory stands in for whatever a project's dependency install produces.

`nen/contract.json` declares `{ "kind": "path", "value": "deps" }` as a
precondition of the `web` lane, so this file existing is what makes that
assertion pass -- and deleting it is what makes the refusal provable.

It is called `deps/` rather than the obvious name because the obvious name is
in this repository's `.gitignore`, and a fixture that cannot be committed
proves nothing.
